{
  "$comment": "Personal overrides for Claude Code. Copy to settings.local.json (gitignored). The Claude Code harness authenticates via `claude login` — do not put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here, that silently switches the harness to API billing. The application reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from .env (see env.example).",
  "$comment_model": "`model` is a personal choice, so it lives here rather than in the committed settings.json (a project-level `model` re-applies on every launch and overrides each user's /model pick). `opusplan` = Opus while planning, Sonnet while executing. Delete the key to keep the account default.",
  "model": "opusplan",
  "$comment_permissions": "`Bash(curl *)` / `Bash(wget *)` are NOT denied by default — `python:*` isn't either, so a Bash-permission deny gave a false sense of coverage. Add \"Bash(curl:*)\" to permissions.allow below to stop the prompt for curl.",
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash(open:*)"
    ]
  },
  "$comment_sandbox": "Permission rules are prefix matches on the command text, not a security boundary: `Bash(rm -rf:*)` does not see `/bin/rm -rf` or `bash -c 'rm -rf ..'`, and a `Read(.env)` deny does not stop a Python one-liner from opening the file. The OS-level control is the sandbox below (macOS Seatbelt built in; Linux/WSL2 need bubblewrap + socat). The filesystem lists mirror AGENTS.md's forbidden paths. Caveat: the app itself reads `.env` via load_dotenv(), so with `.env` in denyRead the CLI, `/llm-test` and examples/ fail inside sandboxed Bash — either run those outside the sandbox / export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the shell instead, or drop `.env` from denyRead and rely on the Read/Edit deny rules for it. The network allowlist has no one-size-fits-all value — tune it to what this project's tooling actually calls (Jira host, npm registry, …) before running unattended somewhere exfiltration risk matters, then set `enabled` to true.",
  "sandbox": {
    "enabled": false,
    "filesystem": {
      "denyRead": [".env", ".env.*", ".envrc", "secrets"],
      "denyWrite": ["data/raw", "models", ".git/hooks"]
    },
    "network": {
      "allowedDomains": [
        "api.anthropic.com",
        "github.com",
        "*.githubusercontent.com",
        "pypi.org",
        "files.pythonhosted.org"
      ]
    }
  }
}
